From fece752d37d680e8606e2cf91f89d984bec7cd31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 04:44:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(review): isolate mirror scenes from render_scale
 hints

Review findings on the render_scale feature commit:

- F1: a window-capture mirror scene wraps the same client surfaces on a
  synthetic output and drove their scale hints. Keep membership,
  enter/leave and suspended bookkeeping for capture frame pacing, but
  publish hints only from scenes with a preferred-scale provider, and
  exclude unbound (mirror) outputs from the derivation; the server
  provider answers -1.0 for them.
- F2: derivation started at 1 and dropped legal sub-1 render scales;
  start at 0 and fall back to 1 only when nothing is derivable.
- F3: warn when render_scale undershoots the logical scale even when
  `scale` is omitted (compare against the documented 1.0 default).
- F4: docs -- direct-scanout exclusion is emergent (hint-following
  buffers no longer match the output mode), not a policy carve-out.
- F5: docs -- "one pixel per rendered pixel" wording for render_scale.

Pin the behavior: config_load warns and honors a sub-scale render_scale
while staying silent when omitted; harness protocol/render_scale phase 3
checks the 60/120 hint split with a 200x150 buffer and phase 4
round-trips workspace-next/previous to fire scene re-derivation.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
